@name Explainer 7: Cooke triplet re-optimised for 2.5 m
# Explainer #7: the Cooke triplet of lenses/cooke-triplet.lens re-optimised
# for an object at 2.5 m: same glasses (N-SK16 / F2 / N-SK16), same structure,
# iris behind the middle element, f/3.5.
# Role: a strong negative lens where the beam is narrow flattens the field;
# three elements just balance the seven classic aberrations.
# Design: all six curvatures, the three glass thicknesses and the air gaps
# (stop position included) vary (EFL 50 mm), minimising the white-light RMS
# spot at 0, 0.5, 0.7 and 1.0 of the field, object at 2.5 m;
# vignetting towards the corner up to half the light.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/explainer/07-triplet.toml`.
# RMS spot (F, e, C) at f/3.5, object at 2.5 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 5.2, 0.5: 18.0, 0.7: 23.8, 1: 10.4 µm. Units: mm.
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
